# AZU-0019, AZU-0021, AZU-0024: all three check for
# log_connections/connection_throttling/log_checkpoints server
# parameters, and all three only recognize the deprecated
# azurerm_postgresql_server resource, not
# azurerm_postgresql_flexible_server (confirmed by inspecting the cached
# policy source — none mention "flexible"). Verified against the real
# server's actual parameters (`az postgres flexible-server parameter
# list`): log_connections and log_checkpoints already default to "on" on
# PostgreSQL 16 Flexible Server (a Terraform resource setting them to
# "on" would be a no-op), and connection_throttling isn't a valid
# parameter on this resource/version at all (confirmed via a real
# ParameterNotExists apply error, not just theory).
AZU-0019
AZU-0021
AZU-0024

# AZU-0013 (Key Vault network ACL default-deny) and AZU-0012 (storage
# account network default-deny): both would block Terraform's own
# apply (running from a laptop, no fixed egress IP) and the app's
# runtime access to Blob (Container Apps isn't VNet-integrated for
# Blob/Key Vault egress). RBAC is this project's actual access-control
# layer for both resources, per D3.3 — reasoning documented at each
# resource in modules/key_vault/main.tf and modules/storage/main.tf.
AZU-0012
AZU-0013

# AZU-0058 (storage GRS): explicitly rejected in Phase 3 — not covered
# by the free grant, costs more, for a dev environment with disposable
# data.
AZU-0058

# AZU-0060, AZU-0061 (storage customer-managed keys, infrastructure/
# double encryption): enterprise-grade controls with no real threat
# model at this project's scale — Microsoft-managed keys are the
# correct default here.
AZU-0060
AZU-0061

# AZU-0057 (storage account logging): genuinely worth having, deferred
# to Phase 8 (observability) — needs a Log Analytics workspace as a
# diagnostic-setting destination, which doesn't exist yet in Phase 4.
AZU-0057

# AZU-0016 (Key Vault purge protection): deliberately off — this is a
# teardown-heavy dev project (Phase 4's whole point is destroy/apply
# cycles), and purge protection would block recreating a same-named
# vault for 90 days after a destroy. Documented at the resource in
# modules/key_vault/main.tf.
AZU-0016

# AZU-0017 (secret expiry date): the database_url secret is regenerated
# on every terraform apply/destroy cycle in this dev project — an
# expiry date adds a real failure mode (secret becomes unusable
# mid-project if forgotten) with no meaningful security benefit at this
# threat model.
AZU-0017
